    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When my nephew was a kid, he was crazy about collecting and trading cards. Whether it was "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Hongmao and Lantu"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "My Little Pony"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", he believed that each one would give him superpowers—or at least make him the coolest kid on the playground. And the money he spent? Let’s just say he could have bought himself a small island. But hey, who needs an island when you have a rare, shiny Hongmao card?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now that he’s older (and maybe a little wiser), he can’t believe how much he once cared about those cards. But he wasn’t alone in his love for them. Kids have been collecting cards for generations. It’s all about fitting in and being part of the “club”. Nothing says “I "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "belong",
            "ref": "v-belong"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” quite like pulling out a pack of these cards."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But there’s a dark side to all that shiny cardboard. Take the current card-collecting craze here in China. Schools are turning into trading floors faster than you can say “limited edition”. Parents and teachers are left "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "scratching their heads",
            "ref": "v-scratch-head"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " while kids fill their pockets with newly found “treasures”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It’s not just about the cards, though; it’s about the exciting search, the social "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pecking order",
            "zh": "社会等级制度"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and the thrill of tearing open a new pack. With the newest anime or video game characters on them, these cards are meant to catch and hold kids’ interest. And because they’re often sold in “blind boxes”, you never know what you’re going to get. They’re like "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "scratch-off lottery tickets",
            "zh": "刮刮乐彩票"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for kids; instead of money, you win "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bragging",
            "zh": "吹嘘"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " rights."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "All this can turn into an expensive, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "vicious cycle",
            "zh": "恶性循环"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Don’t have the card you want? Buy more packs! Still no luck? Trade like your life depends on it! Sound familiar? Maybe it’s time to think about how far you would go—and whether it’s worth it—to complete your collection!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
